{"type":"text","timestamp":1787412733740,"sessionID":"ses_fd5e7cfd4ffeOqqpgv74UZAkcv","part":{"id":"prt_02a19d3c7001SwlVp0ouYP9NBg","messageID":"msg_02a19c2a2001QULt2VTtRxS4CM","sessionID":"ses_fd5e7cfd4ffeOqqpgv74UZAkcv","type":"text","text":"All requirements are satisfied. The change is contained entirely in `lib/glob-match.js`:\n\n- `globMatch(glob, options)` now reads `options.ignore` (string or array) and `options.onResult`/`options.onMatch`/`options.onIgnore`.\n- The ignore matcher is built from `ignoreOpts` with the callbacks and `ignore` stripped out, so the ignore pattern is evaluated without inheriting the caller's callbacks and without recursive ignore.\n- In the matcher, a pattern-match that also matches the ignore pattern is downgraded to a non-match (`finalIsMatch = false`, `ignored = true`); `onResult` fires once per input, `onMatch` only for final matches, `onIgnore` only when excluded by ignore. Inputs that never matched the pattern report as non-match (no `onIgnore`).\n- `result.isMatch` reflects the final decision; the object still carries `glob`, `regex`, `input`, `output` (plus `state`, `posix`, `match`).\n- Array patterns are unchanged in their return values; sub-matchers are built with callbacks stripped so callbacks fire only via the single matcher path (preserving the documented array return shape).\n\nPre-existing test failures (5, all in `scan`/`prefix`) exist independently of this change — confirmed via `git stash`.","time":{"start":1787412730824,"end":1787412733731}}}
